{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>If he entices you.</b> הֲסָתָה is nothing other than incitement, as it is said (I Samuel 26) ״אִם ה׳ הֱסִיתְךָ בִּי״; אנסיטר״א בְּלַעַז — one who influences him to do so." "<b>Your brother.</b> From your father." "Or <b>the son of your mother.</b> From your mother." "<b>Your bosom.</b> She who reclines in your bosom and is joined to you; אפקיי״דא בְּלַעַז. And likewise (Ezekiel 43) ״וּמֵחֵיק הָאָרֶץ״ — from the foundation set in the earth." "<b>Who is as your own soul.</b> This is your father. Scripture spells out for you those who are beloved to you — קַ״וָּ for others." "<b>In secret.</b> Scripture spoke in the present tense, for the words of a seducer are only in secret — and so Solomon says (Proverbs 7): ״בְּנֶשֶׁף בְּעֶרֶב יוֹם בְּאִישׁוֹן לַיְלָה וַאֲפֵלָה״." "<b>Which you have not known, you and your fathers.</b> This is a great disgrace to you — that even the nations do not abandon what their fathers handed down to them, yet this one says to you: abandon what your fathers handed down to you (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "the la'az is Old French inciter, 'to incite'", 3 "the la'az is Old French 'acoller' or similar, 'to embrace/clasp'; the root חיק is read as 'bosom' in both the literal and the transferred sense"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:46:59.773668908Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}